{
  "introText": "Fifty mixed problems spanning all ten chapters, ordered roughly from limits to series and tagged by difficulty. Click any problem to reveal a complete worked solution.",
  "items": [
    {
      "number": "P1",
      "question": {
        "en": "Evaluate \\( \\displaystyle\\lim_{x\\to 2}\\frac{x^2-4}{x-2} \\).",
        "ar": null
      },
      "solution": {
        "en": "<p>Factor: \\( x^2-4=(x-2)(x+2) \\). Cancel \\( (x-2) \\):</p>\\[ \\lim_{x\\to 2}(x+2)=4. \\]",
        "ar": null
      },
      "difficulty": "Basic"
    },
    {
      "number": "P2",
      "question": {
        "en": "Differentiate \\( f(x)=5x^4-3x^2+7 \\).",
        "ar": null
      },
      "solution": {
        "en": "<p>Apply the power and sum rules term by term:</p>\\[ f'(x)=20x^3-6x. \\]",
        "ar": null
      },
      "difficulty": "Basic"
    },
    {
      "number": "P3",
      "question": {
        "en": "Differentiate \\( y=\\dfrac{x}{x^2+1} \\).",
        "ar": null
      },
      "solution": {
        "en": "<p>Quotient rule with \\( f=x,\\ g=x^2+1 \\), so \\( f'=1,\\ g'=2x \\):</p>\\[ y'=\\frac{(1)(x^2+1)-(x)(2x)}{(x^2+1)^2}=\\frac{1-x^2}{(x^2+1)^2}. \\]",
        "ar": null
      },
      "difficulty": "Intermediate"
    },
    {
      "number": "P4",
      "question": {
        "en": "Differentiate \\( y=e^{2x}\\cos x \\).",
        "ar": null
      },
      "solution": {
        "en": "<p>Product rule; the first factor needs the chain rule, \\( \\tfrac{d}{dx}e^{2x}=2e^{2x} \\):</p>\\[ y'=2e^{2x}\\cos x - e^{2x}\\sin x = e^{2x}\\big(2\\cos x-\\sin x\\big). \\]",
        "ar": null
      },
      "difficulty": "Intermediate"
    },
    {
      "number": "P5",
      "question": {
        "en": "Evaluate \\( \\displaystyle\\int_1^{3}\\big(2x+1\\big)\\,dx \\).",
        "ar": null
      },
      "solution": {
        "en": "<p>Antiderivative \\( x^2+x \\). By the Fundamental Theorem:</p>\\[ \\big[x^2+x\\big]_1^{3}=(9+3)-(1+1)=12-2=10. \\]",
        "ar": null
      },
      "difficulty": "Basic"
    },
    {
      "number": "P6",
      "question": {
        "en": "Find the area under \\( f(x)=\\sin x \\) over \\( \\big[0,\\tfrac{\\pi}{2}\\big] \\).",
        "ar": null
      },
      "solution": {
        "en": "<p>Use \\( \\int \\sin x\\,dx=-\\cos x \\):</p>\\[ \\int_0^{\\pi/2}\\sin x\\,dx=\\big[-\\cos x\\big]_0^{\\pi/2}=0-(-1)=1. \\]",
        "ar": null
      },
      "difficulty": "Intermediate"
    },
    {
      "number": "P7",
      "question": {
        "en": "Differentiate \\( y=\\big(3x^2+1\\big)^{5} \\).",
        "ar": null
      },
      "solution": {
        "en": "<p>Chain rule: outer power \\( u^5 \\) gives \\( 5u^4 \\); inner derivative \\( \\tfrac{d}{dx}(3x^2+1)=6x \\):</p>\\[ y'=5\\big(3x^2+1\\big)^{4}\\cdot 6x=30x\\big(3x^2+1\\big)^{4}. \\]",
        "ar": null
      },
      "difficulty": "Advanced"
    },
    {
      "number": "P8",
      "question": {
        "en": "A particle's position is \\( s(t)=t^3-6t^2+9t \\). Find the times when it is momentarily at rest.",
        "ar": null
      },
      "solution": {
        "en": "<p>Velocity is the derivative; rest means \\( v(t)=0 \\):</p>\\[ v(t)=s'(t)=3t^2-12t+9=3(t-1)(t-3). \\]<p>So the particle is at rest at \\( t=1 \\) and \\( t=3 \\).</p>",
        "ar": null
      },
      "difficulty": "Advanced"
    },
    {
      "number": "P9",
      "question": {
        "en": "Find and classify the local extrema of \\( f(x)=2x^3-9x^2+12x \\).",
        "ar": null
      },
      "solution": {
        "en": "<p>\\( f'(x)=6x^2-18x+12=6(x-1)(x-2) \\), so critical points at \\( x=1,2 \\). With \\( f''(x)=12x-18 \\):</p>\\[ f''(1)=-6&lt;0\\ (\\text{max}),\\quad f''(2)=6&gt;0\\ (\\text{min}). \\]<p>Local maximum \\( (1,5) \\), local minimum \\( (2,4) \\).</p>",
        "ar": null
      },
      "difficulty": "Advanced"
    },
    {
      "number": "P10",
      "question": {
        "en": "Evaluate \\( \\displaystyle\\int x\\sin\\!\\big(x^2\\big)\\,dx \\).",
        "ar": null
      },
      "solution": {
        "en": "<p>Let \\( u=x^2 \\), so \\( du=2x\\,dx \\) and \\( x\\,dx=\\tfrac12\\,du \\):</p>\\[ \\int x\\sin\\!\\big(x^2\\big)\\,dx=\\tfrac12\\int\\sin u\\,du=-\\tfrac12\\cos\\!\\big(x^2\\big)+C. \\]",
        "ar": null
      },
      "difficulty": "Intermediate"
    },
    {
      "number": "P11",
      "question": {
        "en": "Find the area enclosed between \\( y=4-x^2 \\) and \\( y=x+2 \\).",
        "ar": null
      },
      "solution": {
        "en": "<p>Intersections: \\( 4-x^2=x+2\\Rightarrow x^2+x-2=0\\Rightarrow x=-2,1 \\). The parabola is on top, so</p>\\[ \\int_{-2}^{1}\\big[(4-x^2)-(x+2)\\big]\\,dx=\\int_{-2}^{1}\\big(2-x-x^2\\big)\\,dx=\\frac{9}{2}. \\]",
        "ar": null
      },
      "difficulty": "Advanced"
    },
    {
      "number": "P12",
      "question": {
        "en": "Evaluate \\( \\displaystyle\\sum_{n=1}^{\\infty} 3\\Big(\\tfrac{1}{4}\\Big)^{n} \\).",
        "ar": null
      },
      "solution": {
        "en": "<p>The first term (at \\( n=1 \\)) is \\( a=\\tfrac34 \\) and the ratio is \\( r=\\tfrac14 \\):</p>\\[ \\sum_{n=1}^{\\infty} 3\\Big(\\tfrac14\\Big)^{n}=\\frac{a}{1-r}=\\frac{3/4}{3/4}=1. \\]",
        "ar": null
      },
      "difficulty": "Intermediate"
    },
    {
      "number": "P13",
      "question": {
        "en": "Solve the separable equation \\( \\dfrac{dy}{dx}=\\dfrac{x}{y} \\).",
        "ar": null
      },
      "solution": {
        "en": "<p>Separate: \\( y\\,dy=x\\,dx \\). Integrate both sides:</p>\\[ \\tfrac{y^2}{2}=\\tfrac{x^2}{2}+C\\ \\Longrightarrow\\ y^2-x^2=C. \\]",
        "ar": null
      },
      "difficulty": "Intermediate"
    },
    {
      "number": "P14",
      "question": {
        "en": "For \\( x=t^2,\\ y=t^3 \\), find \\( \\dfrac{dy}{dx} \\).",
        "ar": null
      },
      "solution": {
        "en": "\\[ \\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{dy/dt}{dx/dt}=\\frac{3t^2}{2t}=\\frac{3t}{2}. \\]",
        "ar": null
      },
      "difficulty": "Intermediate"
    },
    {
      "number": "P15",
      "question": {
        "en": "Evaluate \\( \\displaystyle\\lim_{x\\to 0}\\frac{1-\\cos x}{x^2} \\).",
        "ar": null
      },
      "solution": {
        "en": "<p>Form \\( \\tfrac00 \\); apply L'Hôpital twice:</p>\\[ \\lim_{x\\to 0}\\frac{1-\\cos x}{x^2}=\\lim_{x\\to 0}\\frac{\\sin x}{2x}=\\lim_{x\\to 0}\\frac{\\cos x}{2}=\\frac12. \\]",
        "ar": null
      },
      "difficulty": "Advanced"
    },
    {
      "number": "P16",
      "question": {
        "en": "Evaluate \\( \\displaystyle\\lim_{x\\to 2}\\big(3x^2-x+1\\big) \\).",
        "ar": null
      },
      "solution": {
        "en": "<p>The polynomial is continuous, so substitute directly:</p>\\[ 3(2)^2-2+1=11. \\]",
        "ar": null
      },
      "difficulty": "Basic"
    },
    {
      "number": "P17",
      "question": {
        "en": "Evaluate \\( \\displaystyle\\lim_{x\\to 0}\\frac{\\sin 3x}{x} \\).",
        "ar": null
      },
      "solution": {
        "en": "<p>Use \\( \\lim_{u\\to 0}\\tfrac{\\sin u}{u}=1 \\):</p>\\[ \\lim_{x\\to 0}\\frac{\\sin 3x}{x}=3\\lim_{x\\to 0}\\frac{\\sin 3x}{3x}=3. \\]",
        "ar": null
      },
      "difficulty": "Basic"
    },
    {
      "number": "P18",
      "question": {
        "en": "Evaluate \\( \\displaystyle\\lim_{x\\to\\infty}\\frac{2x^2-3x+1}{5x^2+x} \\).",
        "ar": null
      },
      "solution": {
        "en": "<p>Divide by \\( x^2 \\); lower-order terms vanish, leaving the ratio of leading coefficients:</p>\\[ \\frac{2}{5}. \\]",
        "ar": null
      },
      "difficulty": "Intermediate"
    },
    {
      "number": "P19",
      "question": {
        "en": "Evaluate \\( \\displaystyle\\lim_{x\\to 0}\\frac{\\sqrt{x+4}-2}{x} \\).",
        "ar": null
      },
      "solution": {
        "en": "<p>Multiply by the conjugate \\( \\sqrt{x+4}+2 \\):</p>\\[ \\lim_{x\\to 0}\\frac{(x+4)-4}{x\\big(\\sqrt{x+4}+2\\big)}=\\lim_{x\\to 0}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x+4}+2}=\\frac14. \\]",
        "ar": null
      },
      "difficulty": "Intermediate"
    },
    {
      "number": "P20",
      "question": {
        "en": "Find \\( k \\) so that \\( f(x)=\\begin{cases} x^2,&x\\le 1\\\\ kx,&x&gt;1\\end{cases} \\) is continuous at \\( x=1 \\).",
        "ar": null
      },
      "solution": {
        "en": "<p>The two pieces must agree at \\( x=1 \\): \\( 1^2=k(1) \\).</p>\\[ k=1. \\]",
        "ar": null
      },
      "difficulty": "Intermediate"
    },
