    {
      "number": "P34",
      "question": {
        "en": "A 10 m ladder leans on a wall; its base slides away at 1 m/s. How fast is the top sliding down when the base is 6 m from the wall?",
        "ar": null
      },
      "solution": {
        "en": "<p>From \\( x^2+y^2=100 \\), at \\( x=6 \\) we get \\( y=8 \\). Differentiate: \\( 2x\\,x'+2y\\,y'=0 \\):</p>\\[ y'=-\\frac{x\\,x'}{y}=-\\frac{6(1)}{8}=-0.75\\ \\text{m/s}. \\]<p>The top slides down at \\( 0.75 \\) m/s.</p>",
        "ar": null
      },
      "difficulty": "Advanced"
